# The one-sided route-grid test (docs/issues/live-rig.md, Phase 11): arena pair 406 with the prediction copy
# switched off on machine B only, so that machine A's copy alone asks for routes when the closing cutscene
# walks the players. A prelude for fuzz.py, after the character lines of pair-chars.rig:
#
#   cat tools/rig/examples/pair-chars.rig tools/rig/examples/prelude-route.rig > local/rig-out/route.rig
#   python3 -I -B tools/rig/fuzz.py --states local/rig-out/run4 --out local/rig-out/route --seeds 406:1 \
#       --frames 14000 --levels drunare --groups move,fight,cast,potion,use,dpad,select --no-rerun --keep \
#       --bus "none;delay=4,jitter=3,loss=50" --prelude local/rig-out/route.rig \
#       --patches "FIXES+Net test: item records start from zero, not from stack leftovers" \
#       --extra "--tick-watch pqw=g_pathQueueWrite:s32 --tick-watch pqr=g_pathQueueRead:s32 \
#                --tick-watch pqueue=g_pathQueue:crc6144 --tick-watch pgrid=[[g_world]+0x38]:crc14300"
#
# pgrid is the route grid of this level, one word per node, 65 x 55 nodes. Seen: from tick 11718, machine A's
# copy's first request, the grid differs between the machines in the search marks of 418 nodes until the
# level ends; the queue indexes differ from the same tick. Without the next line both copies ask, at
# different ticks, and the columns differ as well.
B: pnach patches/SLUS-20973_4028A55F.pnach "Arena diagnostic: no prediction copy"

# machine A's player walks into the trigger strip; the opening cutscene; then fuzz.py's random input
A: stick L 0 128
wait 60
A: stick L 128 128
wait 20
A: stick L 128 0
wait 60
A: stick L 128 128
until 0x44fcd0:u8 != 0 timeout 900
until 0x44fcd0:u8 == 0 timeout 4000
